<Base title="About" description="I design products. I've been doing it for five years.">
  <main>
    <h1>ABOUT</h1>
    <p>I'm Nikita.</p>

    <p>
      I design products. I've been doing it for five years.<br />
      Long enough to trust what I see, short enough to keep questioning it.
    </p>
    <p>
      I studied business, not design. I started designing because of
      a project of my own: I felt nobody else would get how I wanted it
      to look. Then came work for friends, then a website for a local
      repair and tailoring studio. It's still live.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then Medal, a desktop app for gamers. I worked on avatars and
      rewards, then on how you record the thing that just happened.
      Then crypto: a wallet, an explorer, a set of tools. None of it is
      running now, for reasons that had nothing to do with design.
      It taught me more than the shipping did.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've tried teams and I've tried agencies. Now I design alone,
      by choice. The work I'm proudest of came when the decisions
      were mine to make.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p>
      Georgia is my second home. I don't speak Georgian, but every time
      I'm there, I understand the place a little better.
    </p>
    <p>
      I reply to designers on X more than I post. I build my own tools
      with Claude Code. I'm trying to make design experiments a habit,
      and every one of them goes public.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p>This week I'm probably:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>picking between two shades of emerald for this site</li>
      <li>building a tool I was missing</li>
      <li>replying on X instead of posting</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <p>
      That's about it.<br />
      If you want to work together —
    </p>
    <a href="/#review">Send a link, get a video review →</a>
  </main>
</Base>

